          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. What is a WebSocket",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==WebSocket== (RFC 6455) = one **long-lived** TCP connection",
            "==Full duplex==: client and server each send at any time",
            "`ws://` → port 80 · `wss://` → TLS on port 443",
            "Starts as HTTP, then switches to binary frames"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. The Opening Handshake",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "GET /chat HTTP/1.1",
            "Upgrade: websocket",
            "Connection: Upgrade",
            "Sec-WebSocket-Key: dGhlIHNh==",
            "Sec-WebSocket-Version: 13"
          ],
          "note": "a plain HTTP/1.1 GET"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "HTTP/1.1 101 Switching Protocols",
            "Upgrade: websocket",
            "Connection: Upgrade",
            "Sec-WebSocket-Accept: s3pPLM="
          ],
          "note": "after 101 → no more HTTP"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Server appends the fixed ==GUID== `258EAFA5-…-C5AB0DC85B11` to the key",
            "Accept = `base64(SHA1(key + GUID))`, proving it speaks WS",
            "After **101** the socket carries only WebSocket frames"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Frames on the Wire",
          "ink": "blue"
